Subject: [PATCH] Standing re-pins never merge; merge-guard required; red index
 main pauses the train
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner cards, 2026-11-13 (about 21:35Z):
- "C. No auto-merge", replacing "A. MM dispatches, auto-merge OK": a
  standing re-pin run opens or updates its PR, labels it needs-repin, and
  never merges itself; the merge manager judges it once CI is green and
  merges. Measured: the self-merges landed 3-4 s after opening, before any
  check.
- "A. merge-guard required status": once the tools workflow posts the
  merge-guard status, the merge manager requires it on main in the layer
  repositories.
- "A. #3119, fix main, pause": while the index main is red, the merge
  manager disables the re-pin train, and re-enables it once green.
In merge-manager-watcher (§"Only the merge manager merges and re-pins"
items 4, 6, 7; the main-red row; the tools follow-ups) and remote-mount
§"Standing consent".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPc2tT1vUufdyDbQTBz
